<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct household spending down 1.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct household spending down 1.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's household spending fell 1.5 percent in October in real terms from a year earlier to an average 314,080 yen per household, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of year-on-year percentage changes in real and nominal terms follows:</p>
<p>				    OCTOBER		SEPTEMBER</p>
<p>				    Real   Nominal     Real  Nominal</p>
<p> Overall household spending -1.5   -1.2	  -4.4    -4.6</p>
<p>(average 314,080 yen)</p>
<p> Spending by wage earners   -0.1   +0.2	  -4.5    -4.7</p>
<p>(average 336,150 yen)</p>
</text>
